 "title": "The Little Way",
 "dates": "Tuesday, September 29 – Sunday, October 4, 2009",
 "logline": "A letter from Trumbull on Michaelmas, a night in the Delgado laundry room that doesn’t stay there, a third date Jack asks for and pays for, and a deaf greyhound at the Blessing of the Animals.",
 "previously": [
  {
   "text": "On the roof at dawn: “Sunday, at the tower, Jack. I didn’t finish a sentence.” You told her you’d noticed. “I know you did.”",
   "if": "e7_sentence==\"noticed\""
  },
  {
   "text": "Wes has a ticket for Columbus Day weekend. “He wants to see the Pacific. I told him it’s a threat.” You said okay.",
   "if": "wes_visit_known && e7_wes==\"okay\""
  },
  {
   "text": "“That a Man and a Woman Can Be Friends.” “That They Can’t.” You won it arguing her side. “I’ll never forgive you.”",
   "if": "duel.friend.rigor>=3"
  },
  {
   "text": "On the bleachers Becca asked if you ever think it might not be true. You told her about two in the morning. “Then I’ll pray for two in the morning.”",
   "if": "e7_doubt==\"twoam\""
  },
  {
   "text": "At Sully’s, Becca texted that she’d saved you a maple bar. Lena: “Then go eat it, dish man.” You stayed.",
   "if": "e7_sun==\"sullys\""
  },
  {
   "text": "Under your door, your paper, in her red. Beside the friend who argues like a prosecutor: *Defense.*"
  }
 ],
